-- RLS step 2b: per-table policies for the `authenticated` role.
-- (Trov #115; plan: docs/security/rls-step2-plan.md §1.2–§1.6, §6.1.
-- Generated by docs/security/rls-step2/gen_policies.py `policies`; edit the
-- generator, not this body, and only ever in a NEW migration once applied.)
--
-- What this does
-- --------------
-- Creates 137 policies on 55 public tables, every one `TO authenticated` and
-- anchored on `(SELECT app_auth.uid())` from step 2a
-- (20261108092633_rls_app_auth_helpers.sql), which is non-NULL only for a JWT
-- the backend minted (iss = 'sapling-api'). The SELECT wrapper makes Postgres
-- evaluate it once per statement (initPlan), not per row. No policy calls
-- auth.uid() (it casts sub to uuid and raises 22P02 on `user_<google id>`).
--
-- Buckets (every one of the 68 public tables is in exactly one; the
-- generator's `check` mode and tests/integration/test_rls_policies_db.py
-- both enforce it):
--   A owned directly (23): users, user_profiles, user_settings, oauth_tokens,
--     gradescope_credentials, enrollments, documents, notes, flashcards,
--     sessions, quiz_attempts, quiz_context, study_guides, graph_nodes,
--     graph_edges, feedback, issue_reports, user_achievements, user_cosmetics,
--     user_roles, xp_events, friend_requests, friendships.
--     Own-row predicate (`user_id = U`, `id = U` for users; either party for
--     friend_requests / friendships), only for the commands step 2c grants.
--   B owned through a parent (9): messages (sessions), node_mastery_events
--     (graph_nodes), note_concepts (notes AND graph_nodes), quiz_responses
--     (quiz_attempts), gradebook_categories, assignments,
--     gradescope_course_links, topic_checklists, topic_checklist_progress
--     (enrollments, via SECURITY DEFINER app_auth.owns_enrollment()).
--   C shared (12): rooms (public, own, or member), room_members (own row or
--     co-member; join only self, unbanned, public-or-own room; leave self or
--     kick as owner), room_bans (owner writes; owner or banned user reads),
--     room_reactions / room_activity (room members), room_summaries (members,
--     read-only), offering_concept_stats / offering_summary (students enrolled
--     in that offering, read-only), course_chunks (shared, own upload, or a
--     contributor; mirrors match_course_chunks), course_chunk_contributors
--     (own), course_chunk_sources (chunk readable). room_messages is bucket C
--     but deliberately has NO policy here: it moves with the step-2e realtime
--     JWT bridge. room_reactions' policies read room_messages as the caller,
--     so where room_messages has RLS on and no policy (production) reactions
--     stay invisible to a user token until 2e adds one.
--   D catalog (12): schools, terms, courses, course_offerings, achievements,
--     achievement_triggers, achievement_cosmetics, cosmetics, roles,
--     role_cosmetics, growth_stages, xp_rules. SELECT when app_auth.uid() IS
--     NOT NULL, i.e. any backend-minted user token.
--   E service-only (12): events, llm_usage, feature_flags,
--     feature_flag_targets, admin_audit_log, email_broadcasts, email_sends,
--     email_suppressions, newsletter_emails, job_applications,
--     encryption_key_check, schema_migrations. No policy, no grant: #807's
--     state (RLS on, nothing for anon/authenticated) is already final.
--
-- Two changes from the plan's appendix draft, both own-row only (see the
-- generator's History): rooms SELECT also admits `owner_id = U`, and
-- room_members SELECT also admits `user_id = U`. PostgREST inserts with
-- `Prefer: return=representation`, so a new row must pass the table's SELECT
-- policy; without these, creating a private room and joining any room failed
-- the RETURNING (is_room_member() is STABLE and cannot see the row the same
-- statement inserts). Verified in a replayed container.
--
-- Why it is inert
-- ---------------
-- * The backend reaches PostgREST as service_role (db/connection.py), which
--   has BYPASSRLS; db/migrate.py, the oracles and the integration conftest
--   connect as `postgres`, the table owner (#807 does not FORCE RLS). Policies
--   never apply to either.
-- * `authenticated` holds no table privileges until step 2c (the next
--   migration), so these policies are not reachable through PostgREST yet.
-- * Nothing mints an `iss: sapling-api` JWT until the `db_user_scope` flag
--   ships (a later PR), so app_auth.uid() is NULL for every request today and
--   every policy here evaluates to false/NULL (deny).
--
-- Idempotent: each CREATE POLICY is preceded by DROP POLICY IF EXISTS for the
-- same name (dropping a policy is a metadata change, not a data change), all
-- inside one DO block. The block returns early on a bare Postgres without the
-- `authenticated` role, like the repo's other role-touching migrations. A
-- missing table or column fails the migration (db/migrate.py rolls the batch
-- back), which is the right outcome for schema drift.
--
-- Reverse (by hand, as the migration role). Reverse step 2c FIRST (its header),
-- or `authenticated` is left holding grants with no policies (still deny-all
-- under RLS, but the coverage test fails):
